# Snickerdoodle product rules

Snickerdoodle is Product 2 in the Racoben Engineering portfolio. ShipCheck is Product 1.

## Brand and routes

- Product name: **`PRODUCT_NAME` in `lib/site.ts`** (currently Snickerdoodle) — import everywhere; do not hardcode
- Route: `/snickerdoodle`
- Intake email: `snickerdoodle@racoben.com`
- Tagline: "One survey. A complete campaign package."

## What we sell

Campaign execution packages — not marketing, copy, AI, or templates.

Every package moves one audience toward one clearly defined action.

## Customer-facing scope (V1)

- Campaign survey → polished human-reviewed campaign execution package
- Public CTAs use a monitored fit-check email; qualified prospects receive an expiring, email-bound signed link to the unlisted, no-index survey
- Survey submissions are validated server-side and stored as pending intents in Supabase; no order or payment is created
- No customer auth, customer dashboard, customer-facing AI, or payment runtime
- Preserve the warm cream/green palette, Fraunces/Geist typography, section layout, and shadcn/Tailwind styling with original Snickerdoodle branding only
- Do not re-scaffold or simplify the UI

## Internal production model

```text
Survey → campaign family → desired action → fact ledger → campaign strategy
→ asset map → draft → critique → polish → QA → independent marketing review → package
```

- The service-lead role uses ChatGPT and custom AI tooling to draft/adapt/critique/polish/package
- A prospective independent marketing reviewer is the **final expert quality gate**, not the first drafter
- The reviewer role is unassigned and under HARD HOLD. Do not infer identity, relationship, employment, compensation, ownership, availability, authority, or access.
- This two-person model may activate only after CEO designation and assignment, availability and training confirmation, classification/conflict/IP clearance, least-privilege per-order access approval, two timed synthetic rehearsals, and documented CFO+CRO concurrence for every monetary term.

## Hard rules

- **AI is internal only.** Never customer-facing AI, chat, prompts, or model settings.
- **Fact ledger only.** AI must not invent sponsors, donation matches, statistics, quotes, links, partners, deadlines, outcomes, or claims.
- **Human review required** before every delivery.

## Do not add (V1)

- customer-facing AI
- chat or prompt interfaces
- customer auth or payment integration
- customer dashboard or automated delivery portal
- email sending platform or social posting automation
- analytics that stores personal/project data
- RacobenStudio implementation in this repo

## Key files

- `lib/site.ts` — brand constants, basePath prefix, intake email
- `lib/intake.ts` — survey field model and limits
- `app/api/brief/route.ts` — bounded, origin-checked, idempotent Supabase intake
- `docs/operating-doctrine.md` — product philosophy
- `docs/campaign-families.md` — launch campaign families
- `docs/internal-automation-pipeline.md` — staff production workflow
- `docs/fact-ledger.md` — single source of truth for AI drafting
- `docs/editor-packet.md` — independent marketing review bundle spec
- `fulfillment/` — pipeline, QA, delivery, internal prompts

## Deploy

- Standalone Vercel project with `basePath: '/snickerdoodle'`
- Parent Racoben site rewrites `/snickerdoodle` and `/snickerdoodle/*` via `SNICKERDOODLE_PRODUCTION_URL` (no path suffix in env var)
- The local repo is named Snickerdoodle; the GitHub repository still has the legacy `CauseBrief` name until the owner explicitly authorizes a public rename
